{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The outcomes from both lotteries are: -1000, 0 (from Lottery A) and -500 (from Lottery B). The average outcome is calculated as the unweighted mean of these outcomes: (-1000 + 0 + (-500)) / 3 = -1500 / 3 = -500. Next, we count how many outcomes in each lottery are higher than this average (-500). For Lottery A: 0 is higher than -500 (one outcome), and -1000 is not. So, Lottery A has 1 outcome above the average. For Lottery B: -500 is not higher than -500 (equal, not higher), so it has 0 outcomes above the average. Thus, the decision reason prefers Lottery A, as it has more outcomes above the average (-500) than Lottery B.",
